      "<strong>v1.24.6 &mdash; deriveShell priority flip: spa-owner > rep (was rep > spa-owner) so dual-role users land in their primary shell.</strong> Surfaced when admin impersonated real Karen from the PersonaSwitcher: she resolved to RepShell instead of RefillShell because her <code>user_roles</code> contains BOTH <code>spa_owner</code> (from tenant_memberships) AND <code>rep</code> (from a rep_accounts row, likely origin_type='spa_owner' for attribution-chain reasons). Pre-fix deriveShell priority was admin > rep > spa-owner > developer; rep won. Karen's 1,140 patients + recovery feed never rendered because RepShell took over with her (empty) rep-attribution data instead. Fix: deriveShell priority is now admin > spa-owner > rep > developer. Rationale: in Refill's model, owning a spa tenant is the more concrete primary identity &mdash; that's where the patients, recovery events, billing live. Rep attribution is supplementary infrastructure for referral chains. Pure reps (Kelly, no spa_owner role) stay shell='rep' unchanged. A future user who is PRIMARILY a rep AND happens to own a spa would now land in spa-owner shell by default; they can navigate to /app/rep directly &mdash; minor friction trade-off for the more common case being right by default. Touched: <code>src/server/role-helpers.ts</code> (deriveShell priority order), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
