      "<strong>v1.24.5 &mdash; Rep-platform read fns honor viewAsUserId; Spa Owner persona now points at real Karen for the QuickBooks-uploaded roster.</strong> Two interlocking fixes for the demo walk. <strong>(1) Kelly's rep pages were blank under impersonation</strong> &mdash; <code>useRepProfile</code> + <code>getMyRepAccount</code> were opted into viewAsUserId back in v1.24.0, but the rep-platform's other reads (<code>getMyNetwork</code>, <code>getMyLedger</code>, <code>getMyLiveEarnings</code>, <code>listMyReferralLinks</code>) still resolved by caller and returned admin's empty rep data. Mirror of the v1.23.0 spa-owner long-tail sweep but for the rep platform: each fn now takes an optional <code>viewAsUserId</code> via the shared <code>authWithViewAsInput</code> schema and uses <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> for filtering. Page consumers + <code>LiveEarningsCard</code> + <code>RefillRepHome</code> read <code>getAdminViewAsUserId()</code> from localStorage and plumb through. Net effect: when admin impersonates Kelly, RepShell renders chrome AND inner pages (Network / Recruit / Ledger / Referral Links / Economics / Outreach) populate with her 7 downstream, 64 ledger, 19 outreach, 20 recovery events. <strong>(2) Spa Owner persona retargeted at real Karen.</strong> The v1.24.4 allowlist pointed Spa Owner at <code>karen@rejuv-demo.test</code> (demo tenant 'Rejuv Skin Spa'), which has 17 recovery events seeded but only 1 patient. Grasshopper's QuickBooks customer-sales-detail CSV upload landed under <code>karen.aslak@gmail.com</code> (real Karen, production 'Rejuv' tenant) via the post-v1.20.5 admin-impersonation write path. Result: 1,140 real patients existed in DB but the demo persona pointed at the wrong Karen. v1.24.5 fixes the persona allowlist to use <code>karen.aslak@gmail.com</code>. The Spa Owner walk now renders Karen's actual production patient roster, addresses, transaction history &mdash; the real data we already loaded. <strong>Side note</strong>: the v1.24.5 proposal to seed 75 synthetic patients was wrong &mdash; per <em>feedback-real-data-first</em>, real data structure beats synthetic. Migration file deleted before paste. Touched: <code>src/server/rep-platform.ts</code> (4 fns opted in, shared authWithViewAsInput schema), <code>src/routes/app.rep.network.tsx</code> + <code>app.rep.recruit.tsx</code> + <code>app.rep.ledger.tsx</code> + <code>app.rep.referral-links.tsx</code> + <code>app.rep.economics.tsx</code> + <code>app.rep.outreach.tsx</code> (page-side plumbing), <code>src/components/refill/LiveEarningsCard.tsx</code> + <code>RefillRepHome.tsx</code> (component plumbing), <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code> (real Karen allowlist), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
