      "<strong>v1.24.4 &mdash; PersonaSwitcher restricted to 3 canonical demo personas: Admin (caller) / Spa Owner (Karen Demo) / Rep (Kelly Demo).</strong> Pre-fix, the dropdown listed all 14 users with non-member roles (every spa-owner including production Karen Aslakson, every rep, every developer). Two problems: (1) demo flow diluted &mdash; operator needs THREE personas to walk the system, not fourteen, and (2) production users (real karen.aslak with 1,140 live patients) leaked into the demo switcher when they should be reached only via /app/admin/users for ops work. Per Grasshopper: 'i don't need switcher for users - JUST ROLES'. Fix: new <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code> defines <code>DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS</code> allowlist (<code>karen@rejuv-demo.test</code> + <code>kelly@refill-demo.test</code>). PersonaSwitcher filters the listImpersonableUsers result client-side to caller + allowlisted emails before grouping. Shell-group labels switched to singular (Admin / Spa Owner / Rep) since each group has exactly one persona now. The server fn + /app/admin/users CRUD continue to surface ALL users — that's the operator surface; the dropdown is the demo surface. Adding a fourth demo persona requires deliberately editing demo-personas.ts (not just a DB row), which keeps the dropdown intentional. <strong>Queued (v1.24.5)</strong>: demo data audit + restore. Rejuv Skin Spa demo tenant has 17 recovery events + $3,925 lifetime but only 1 patient — incoherent for a walkthrough. Patient roster + outreach history + downstream tenants need re-seeding to make the demo flow meaningful end-to-end. Touched: <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code> (new allowlist), <code>src/components/admin/PersonaSwitcher.tsx</code> (filter + singular labels), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
