      "<strong>v1.20.7 &mdash; Lane 2 @theme audit: shadcn semantic tokens defined, retroactively unblocking ~700 silently-broken refs across 35 files.</strong> Audit ran the grep against every Tailwind utility class consuming a color name vs. what&rsquo;s actually defined in <code>@theme</code>. Findings: <strong>(a)</strong> primary tokens fully resolved (v1.11&rsquo;s 31-file sweep + v1.20 polish kept it clean — only 4 remaining hits, all inert strings inside changelog HTML or comments); <strong>(b)</strong> <em>massive</em> shadcn-semantic-token gap &mdash; ~700 references to <code>bg-card</code> (102), <code>bg-background</code> (82), <code>text-foreground</code> (160), <code>text-muted-foreground</code> (65), <code>bg-muted</code> + opacity variants (~140), <code>text-destructive</code> (46), <code>divide-border</code> (21), <code>ring-ring</code> (19), <code>border-input</code> (15), <code>bg-destructive/N</code> variants (~36), <code>bg-accent</code> (3), <code>bg-popover</code>, <code>bg-sidebar-accent</code>, <code>text-accent-foreground</code>, <code>text-popover-foreground</code>, etc. ALL emitting zero CSS in Tailwind v4 because none of <code>--color-card</code>, <code>--color-muted</code>, <code>--color-background</code>, <code>--color-foreground</code>, <code>--color-destructive</code>, <code>--color-border</code>, <code>--color-input</code>, <code>--color-ring</code>, <code>--color-accent</code>, <code>--color-popover</code>, <code>--color-sidebar-accent</code> exist in our <code>@theme</code> block. Same class of silently-broken-token bug as the v1.10 primary find + v1.17 rule find &mdash; just at much larger scale. <strong>Three approaches considered</strong>: (A) mechanical sed sweep across 35 files (high blast radius, 700+ replacements, mis-sed risk), (B) sweep only load-bearing routes (leaves long-tail broken), (C) <em>add the missing shadcn semantic role tokens to @theme so they actually render</em> &mdash; same single-styles.css-change pattern v1.17 used to retroactively unblock all rule-* refs. <strong>Picked C</strong> &mdash; it&rsquo;s the same architectural pattern, zero risk of consumer-site mis-sed, single point of truth for what these roles mean visually for the Refill brand. <strong>Implementation</strong>: 16 lines added to <code>src/styles.css</code>&rsquo;s <code>@theme</code> block mapping shadcn semantic roles to Refill brand colors: <code>background</code>&rarr;paper, <code>foreground</code>&rarr;ink, <code>card</code>&rarr;<code>#ffffff</code> (pure white, brighter than warm paper, distinguishes floating surfaces), <code>card-foreground</code>&rarr;ink, <code>popover</code>&rarr;<code>#ffffff</code>, <code>popover-foreground</code>&rarr;ink, <code>muted</code>&rarr;rule-soft (warm off-white for subtle backgrounds), <code>muted-foreground</code>&rarr;ink-soft, <code>accent</code>&rarr;emerald-soft (brand-tinted hover state), <code>accent-foreground</code>&rarr;emerald, <code>destructive</code>&rarr;rose, <code>destructive-foreground</code>&rarr;paper, <code>border</code>&rarr;rule, <code>input</code>&rarr;rule, <code>ring</code>&rarr;emerald (focus matches brand), <code>sidebar-accent</code>&rarr;rule-soft, <code>sidebar-foreground</code>&rarr;ink. <strong>Why this DOESN&rsquo;T conflict with the v1.10 &lsquo;don&rsquo;t add --color-primary&rsquo; decision</strong>: primary was special &mdash; emerald IS the brand primary, so adding the indirection back would have been redundant. card/muted/foreground/destructive/etc. are different &mdash; they&rsquo;re semantic roles (&ldquo;floating surface&rdquo;, &ldquo;less-prominent text&rdquo;, &ldquo;warning state&rdquo;) that need an explicit color mapping per-theme. Defining them just establishes what those roles look like in the Refill brand. <strong>Existing translations stay intact</strong>: every concrete brand-token reference shipped in v1.10/v1.11/v1.14/v1.16/v1.17/v1.20.x (<code>bg-emerald</code>, <code>text-ink</code>, <code>border-rule</code>, etc.) still resolves to the same color &mdash; v1.20.7 only adds NEW token definitions, doesn&rsquo;t modify any existing ones. Visual change is strictly &lsquo;invisible &rarr; visible&rsquo; on previously-broken sites. <strong>Single 16-line styles.css change</strong>: 35-file blast radius eliminated. Touched: <code>src/styles.css</code> (shadcn semantic layer added), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
