      "<strong>v1.18 &mdash; Full password lifecycle: /reset-password (public) + /app/refill/settings/account (gated).</strong> Closes the gap that surfaced during the admin-recovery thread: the /login &lsquo;Forgot password?&rsquo; modal already fires <code>supabase.auth.resetPasswordForEmail({ redirectTo: &quot;https://getrefill.app/reset-password&quot; })</code>, but the redirect target didn&rsquo;t exist as a route &mdash; the recovery email arrived but clicking the link 404&rsquo;d. And there was no in-app change-password UI for already-signed-in users either &mdash; the only path was Supabase Dashboard. v1.18 ships both surfaces. <strong>(a) /reset-password</strong>: public route. Mirrors /login&rsquo;s single-card-centered-paper-bg styling with inline hex colors (same Georgia serif headline, same #056048/#fbfaf7/#e6e2d6 palette). Detects the Supabase auth handoff via <code>supabase.auth.getSession()</code> + listens for <code>PASSWORD_RECOVERY</code> / <code>SIGNED_IN</code> auth events. Four phases: <code>checking</code> (verifying link), <code>invalid</code> (expired/missing tokens &mdash; shows &lsquo;Recovery links expire after one hour&rsquo;), <code>ready</code> (form with new + confirm fields, min 8 chars, eye toggle, real-time mismatch check), <code>done</code> (success card &mdash; signs out the recovery session so the next sign-in is clean, redirects to /login after 1.8s). <strong>(b) /app/refill/settings/account</strong>: auth-gated route. Mirrors the existing settings-page chrome (PageHeader + brand-token Tailwind). Two sections: read-only Email row showing <code>user.email</code> from useAuth() with &lsquo;Contact support to change&rsquo; copy (email change requires reverification flow, deferred), and Change Password card with new + confirm fields + auto &lsquo;Last changed N ago&rsquo; helper text using <code>auth.users.updated_at</code>. On submit calls <code>supabase.auth.updateUser({ password })</code>; success toast + form reset. <strong>UX decision</strong>: no current-password verification field on either page. Supabase&rsquo;s <code>updateUser</code> doesn&rsquo;t require it (the active JWT is the auth gate), and requiring it would be security theater &mdash; if an attacker has the JWT they have the change anyway. Cleaner to skip. <strong>Real-time validation</strong>: both pages show inline &lsquo;Passwords don&rsquo;t match&rsquo; rose text only when confirm has been typed AND mismatches (not on empty); submit button disabled until both fields valid + match. <strong>Eye toggle</strong>: show/hide password using lucide Eye/EyeOff icons, applies to both fields (single toggle controls both). <strong>Surface entry</strong>: /reset-password is reachable from email links (existing flow now works end-to-end) + the &lsquo;Back to sign in&rsquo; link in the page header. /app/refill/settings/account currently reachable via direct URL only; chip nav entry deferred until we decide where it fits per the trojan-horse 4-chip thesis. Touched: <code>src/routes/reset-password.tsx</code> (new file, ~285 lines), <code>src/routes/app.refill.settings.account.tsx</code> (new file, ~220 lines), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
